it is very autobiographical not in terms  of necessarily every moment in the film  but the characters upon which the story  is based these were it was based upon  family members and I I tried to  delineate those complex things that I  saw within my family that made made this  a compelling story for me and hopefully  for you well I was very friendly with  Andie McDowell's agent and he and I  would spend long hours trying to figure  out who to cast in the film and he at  one point said to me I think you should  really consider Andie I know she's not  necessarily someone you would think of  in this role but I think I think she  might be able to do the part and I think  she would enjoy it and I think it would  be something that she'd find challenging  and I met with her and I found in her  fragility that I thought was the essence  of this character and she really wanted  to do the part and she came on board  very excited about it and she knew it  was gonna be a stretch to do the accent  she worked with three different dialect  coaches I finally had her her final  version looked at by Tim Manik who is a  very well-known  dialect coach and he he gave her the  green light and said that she was she  was doing really well I think but has  been hard for some audiences is just  knowing how Andy typically speaks and  then seeing her for the first few  moments can be somewhat jarring but  after Andy came on board  Chaz palm and Terry I got the script to  him I he was really one of my first  choices for the role of of Joe and I  think not and obviously not because he's  Jewish he's not but I thought he could  relate to the character and I thought  that he could play this character and I  thought he was probably one of the few  people out there who could do do justice  to this role because he has such an  ominous quality to him but also such a  lovable quality and I sent it to him and  somehow got it through the  wall of agents that often keeps keeps  low-budget filmmakers from reaching  their cast destinations and he he took a  look at the script and I got a phone  call from him almost immediately that he  wanted to play the role and from there  on in he was so committed and so excited  about the project and I think working  with him has been possibly the greatest  experience of my entire professional  career he is just such first of all in  my opinion a brilliant actor but also I  I would say the quintessential mensch  Chaz sent me an email and it was so nice  I actually hung it up and he said and he  said don't worry about what the critics  say don't worry about what the box  office is we've screened this for enough  people to know that this touches people  and you've made something good here and  I know it will have a life and I thought  that was just so beautiful and so  supportive and I love him for that and  the one thing he asked me along the way  was after helping me in the way that he  did he said to me I just have one  request for you and that is that you  help someone else in the future and  again I thought you know that just shows  the nature of this man and his his  completely generous spirit
 

